# Netlify settings for the I-ITSM website (only used on Netlify; running on your laptop ignores this file).

# 1) Every /api/... request is passed on to our Spring Boot backend on Render.
#    That is why the code can keep using short /api/... paths, and there are no CORS problems.
#    BEFORE YOU BUILD: replace YOUR-BACKEND with the name of your Render service.
/api/*  https://iitsm-backend.onrender.com/api/:splat  200

# 2) Any other address (like /admin/incidents) loads the React app, which then shows the right page.
#    Without this, refreshing a page on Netlify would show "Page not found".
/*  /index.html  200
